      "message": "@ddoman@chromium.org, create new thread here.\n\nSince this may raise lock error if another process is running sync(), I think the timeout should respect the lock_timeout like populate().\nBecause if process A runs populate(), and process B calls contains_revision(), it is easy to hit 20s timeout and the user configured lock_timeout does not take effect. \n\nOr as you said, we could have different lock types for populate and contains_revision. WDYT?",
